{
  "_description": "Domain scope for neuro-ICU ontology cleanup. Curated from all 11 BrainIT papers. Used by built-in cleanup to decide what is in-scope, what to exempt from evidence pruning, and what to allow through abstract/broad filters. Independent of the gold-standard ontology (which is used for evaluation metrics only).",
  "_version": "1.0",
  "_source_papers": [
    "1. Piper 2003 — BrainIT group concept and core dataset definition",
    "2. Moss 2013 — Trusting ICU data (provenance, SSN, RDF)",
    "3. Stell 2018 — Automated measurement of adherence to TBI guidelines",
    "4. Shaw 2024 — PbtO2 and ICP relationship exploration",
    "5. Georgatzis 2016 — Artefact in physiological data (FSLDS)",
    "6. Güiza 2015a — Visualizing pressure and time burden of ICP",
    "7. Donald 2012 — Trigger characteristics of EUSIG-defined hypotensive events",
    "8. Depreitere 2018 — Cerebral perfusion pressure variability",
    "9. Donald 2019 — Forewarning of hypotensive events (Bayesian ANN)",
    "10. Decraene 2023 — Decompressive craniectomy as second/third-tier intervention",
    "11. Güiza 2015b — Visualizing pressure and time burden (variant)"
  ],

